WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:14.806
do you think they took my parents?"

2
00:00:15.327 --> 00:00:16.587
Gliss asked tearfully.

3
00:00:17.368 --> 00:00:18.048
"I don't know."

4
00:00:18.568 --> 00:00:24.031
Zann tried to answer patiently, even though Gliss had asked the same question about fifty times already.

5
00:00:24.051 --> 00:00:25.672
"It'll be okay."

6
00:00:26.112 --> 00:00:27.953
Perda put an arm around Gliss' shoulders.

7
00:00:27.973 --> 00:00:30.175
"We'll figure out how to save them.

8
00:00:30.855 --> 00:00:32.436
And Boz and all the others too."

9
00:00:34.184 --> 00:00:39.146
An hour had passed since Zann had zapped himself, Darb, and Zing to within a few paces of

10
00:00:39.186 --> 00:00:39.607
the Hollow.

11
00:00:40.327 --> 00:00:43.128
Zing had whimpered as soon as he'd realized where they were.

12
00:00:43.849 --> 00:00:47.910
But Darb had coaxed the nervous dragon into following him and Zann into the Hollow.

13
00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:50.772
They'd peered out as Morb appeared.

14
00:00:51.432 --> 00:00:56.254
He'd looked around in confusion, muttered a few angry words, and then zapped himself away again.

15
00:00:58.075 --> 00:00:59.496
Darb's plan had worked!

16
00:01:00.172 --> 00:01:03.995
Being in the Hollow had blocked whatever spell Morb was using to track Zann.

17
00:01:04.675 --> 00:01:07.537
A few minutes later, Perda and Gliss had arrived on foot.

18
00:01:09.518 --> 00:01:12.360
Now it was getting dark, and they were all still in the Hollow.

19
00:01:13.001 --> 00:01:17.744
The Hollow was a low, grassy spot protected by a thick tangle of thorny vines.

20
00:01:18.785 --> 00:01:24.549
The only entrance lay between the gnarled trunks of two ancient mood trees, and nobody who didn't know

21
00:01:24.609 --> 00:01:26.110
it was there would ever notice it.

22
00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:29.352
Not even Morb—whoever he might really be.

23
00:01:30.132 --> 00:01:34.776
"We need to figure out how a Void got such strong magic," Zann said.

24
00:01:34.796 --> 00:01:40.500
"Enough to perform Flash Freezes, and whatever Tracking spell he was using to follow me."

25
00:01:41.661 --> 00:01:42.902
Gliss looked confused.

26
00:01:42.922 --> 00:01:45.824
"How would a Void get any magic at all?"

27
00:01:46.164 --> 00:01:46.625
she asked.

28
00:01:46.645 --> 00:01:48.386
"It's impossible, isn't it?"

29
00:01:48.406 --> 00:01:50.988
"Not totally," Zann said.

30
00:01:51.008 --> 00:01:53.990
"I knew a Void when I lived in First City.

31
00:01:54.651 --> 00:01:59.878
His mom was a Red, and she infused a pair of gloves with a little bit of magic

32
00:01:59.938 --> 00:02:01.259
he could use each day.

33
00:02:01.999 --> 00:02:04.681
Just enough to conjure up lunch and stuff like that."

34
00:02:05.421 --> 00:02:08.403
Zann was surprised that Gliss didn't know about that sort of thing.

35
00:02:09.043 --> 00:02:11.725
Then again, she'd lived in Swamp Bottom all her life.

36
00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:17.728
There were only a few Voids in town, and most seemed content to rely on others for what

37
00:02:17.788 --> 00:02:19.549
little magic they needed to get by.

38
00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:23.952
It was different in the larger towns and cities, where people weren't as neighborly.

39
00:02:24.588 --> 00:02:27.849
"But that's not the kind of magic we're talking about," Perda said.

40
00:02:27.869 --> 00:02:31.290
"No magic-infused glove could do a Flash Freeze.

41
00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.850
The magic would be too weak.

42
00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:36.331
You couldn't even use it to zap yourself six inches away."

43
00:02:36.351 --> 00:02:38.032
"I know."

44
00:02:38.612 --> 00:02:39.892
Zann was thinking hard.

45
00:02:39.912 --> 00:02:45.214
"The Directory said Morb worked in the research lab at the university, remember?

46
00:02:46.114 --> 00:02:49.335
Maybe he learned about some stronger kind of infusion.

47
00:02:50.095 --> 00:02:53.256
Researchers are always working on new forms of magic there."

48
00:02:53.964 --> 00:02:55.045
Perda looked skeptical.

49
00:02:55.065 --> 00:02:59.907
"If researchers were working on something that big, we would've heard about it," she said.

50
00:02:59.927 --> 00:03:03.248
"Every Void in Magica would be lining up to try it.

51
00:03:03.648 --> 00:03:04.188
Right, Darb?"

52
00:03:05.289 --> 00:03:09.731
Darb shrugged and kept petting Zing, who lay beside him looking anxious and miserable.

53
00:03:09.751 --> 00:03:14.073
"I wonder how Morb got those trolls to work with him," Darb said.

54
00:03:14.753 --> 00:03:15.593
Perda shuddered.

55
00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:17.834
"Those trolls were scary!

56
00:03:18.515 --> 00:03:20.015
I never saw a real one before.

57
00:03:20.395 --> 00:03:21.556
Only pictures in books."

58
00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.161
Gliss wasn't paying much attention to the others.

59
00:03:24.181 --> 00:03:27.924
"I can't believe my parents are gone," she moaned.

60
00:03:27.944 --> 00:03:30.065
"We need to find them!"

61
00:03:31.186 --> 00:03:32.567
"I know," Zann said.

62
00:03:32.587 --> 00:03:35.249
"I'm worried about my grandfather too.

63
00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.111
But Morb got a good look at all of us.

64
00:03:38.531 --> 00:03:40.553
Who knows what he'd do if he saw us again?"

65
00:03:40.573 --> 00:03:43.315
"We already know what he'd do to you two."

66
00:03:43.995 --> 00:03:45.616
Perda glanced at Zann and Gliss.

67
00:03:45.916 --> 00:03:47.958
"He'd summon his trolls to carry you off."

68
00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:51.000
Darb stepped toward the entrance and looked out.

69
00:03:51.792 --> 00:03:54.293
"Maybe I should sneak back to town," he suggested.

70
00:03:54.313 --> 00:03:58.014
"I could let our families know what happened and see what I can find out."

71
00:03:58.034 --> 00:04:00.715
"No way," Zann said.

72
00:04:00.735 --> 00:04:02.035
"It's too risky."

73
00:04:02.755 --> 00:04:03.436
Perda nodded.

74
00:04:03.456 --> 00:04:07.197
"If we hide out here for a while, the grown-ups will take care of everything.

75
00:04:07.597 --> 00:04:11.618
Right?" Nobody said anything for a long moment.

76
00:04:12.358 --> 00:04:13.919
Zann felt sick and scared.

77
00:04:14.559 --> 00:04:16.600
He'd always longed for adventure and excitement.

78
00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:17.780
Now he'd found it.

79
00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:21.662
But somehow it wasn't nearly as much fun as he'd imagined it would be.

80
00:04:22.622 --> 00:04:24.563
Darb was still staring out into the night.

81
00:04:25.204 --> 00:04:26.705
"Look!" he said suddenly.

82
00:04:26.725 --> 00:04:28.185
"Here comes a message moth.

83
00:04:28.526 --> 00:04:29.666
We'd better see who it's for."

84
00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:31.307
Zann's heart thumped.

85
00:04:31.707 --> 00:04:33.128
"Are you sure that's a good idea?

86
00:04:33.908 --> 00:04:35.790
What if Morb can track us through it?"

87
00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:37.971
"I doubt it," Perda said.

88
00:04:38.291 --> 00:04:41.633
"Otherwise he would have found me and Gliss when you sent us that message earlier."

89
00:04:41.653 --> 00:04:48.132
"Right. It seemed like his Tracking spell worked by locating the person who was creating the magic," Darb

90
00:04:48.172 --> 00:04:49.473
said in his logical way.

91
00:04:49.493 --> 00:04:54.116
"It probably doesn't track the moth itself, or the person that it's going to."

92
00:04:54.136 --> 00:04:55.837
"I hope you're right."

93
00:04:56.377 --> 00:04:57.998
Zann stepped outside with the others.

94
00:04:58.658 --> 00:05:00.519
The moth immediately fluttered over to him.

95
00:05:01.239 --> 00:05:04.641
He gently held the creature in his hands, peering at it in the moonlight.

96
00:05:04.661 --> 00:05:06.622
"It's from Boz!"

97
00:05:07.023 --> 00:05:09.444
he said when he saw the name etched on one wing.

98
00:05:10.104 --> 00:05:15.367
The message on the other wing was inscribed in Boz's sloppy handwriting, not the neater letters that appeared

99
00:05:15.407 --> 00:05:16.308
when he wrote mentally.

100
00:05:17.032 --> 00:05:18.893
It read: Morb no good.

101
00:05:19.694 --> 00:05:22.615
Find my old diary and show it to palace.

102
00:05:22.636 --> 00:05:24.697
"That means he's alive!"

103
00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:25.637
Perda cried.

104
00:05:25.657 --> 00:05:28.599
"The Reds who disappeared are alive!"

105
00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:30.720
Gliss looked relieved.

106
00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.122
"We have to find them and save them!"

107
00:05:33.902 --> 00:05:35.003
Zann knew she was right.

108
00:05:35.283 --> 00:05:36.624
But it wasn't going to be easy.

109
00:05:37.244 --> 00:05:42.307
To find Boz's diary, they'd have to leave the safety of the Hollow and return to where Zann's

110
00:05:42.347 --> 00:05:42.988
house had been.

111
00:05:43.805 --> 00:05:46.993
Then they would need to figure out how to get to the palace in First City.

112
00:05:47.674 --> 00:05:50.221
And they'd have to do it all without any magic.
